# AI Productivity Assistant — Rules & Conventions

## Architecture

- No VPS. Everything runs on local machine + Claude cloud services.
- Claude Desktop connects to DB directly via MCP tools (stdio mode).
- Claude Mobile creates a JSON artifact, synced to DB on schedule or manual command.
- Express API is the single business logic layer. MCP is an HTTP client wrapping the API — not a logic layer.
- Docker runs the API only. MCP server runs locally via Claude Desktop (stdio spawn).

## Data Sources & Priority

Three parties exist. Priority order (highest to lowest):

1. Google Calendar
2. Claude Task Artifact
3. DB

- DB is never updated directly. All writes go through the artifact.
- Google Calendar always wins over Artifact.
- Artifact always wins over DB.
- Tiebreak: most recent `updated_at` wins.

## Google Calendar Event Mapping

- `estimated_minutes = null or 0` → all-day event (reminder / quick task)
- `estimated_minutes > 0` → timed event: start to start + estimated_minutes
- Completed task → add `[done]` prefix to event title
- Archived task → stays in DB only, never synced to Calendar
- All task metadata is stored in the event `description` field using a `[task]` block:

```
[task]
id: <number>
priority: <1-5>
status: <inbox|scheduled|done>
estimated_minutes: <number>
source: <string>
is_recurring: <0|1>
recur_pattern: <daily|weekly|monthly>
```

- Recurring tasks use native Google Calendar RRULE recurrence.
- Timezone is `Australia/Melbourne` for all timed events.

## Task Status

- Valid flow: `inbox` → `scheduled` → `done`
- Side exit: any status → `archived` (for duplicates or cancelled tasks)
- Never hard-delete tasks. Use `archived` instead.
- `done` and `archived` tasks are excluded from artifact active list.
- Artifact sync query: `status NOT IN ('done', 'archived')`

## Artifact Sync Window

Fetch tasks where:
- `status NOT IN ('done', 'archived')`, AND one of:
  - `is_recurring = 1` (always include, regardless of due date)
  - `due_at IS NULL` (inbox items, no scheduled date)
  - `due_at` within `-3 days` to `+7 days` from now

Recurring tasks are always included to prevent duplicate creation from mobile.

## DB Role (Analytics Only)

- DB is not the primary store in V2. It is the analytics and learning layer.
- Tracks `actual_minutes` vs `estimated_minutes` for learning which task types consistently overrun.
- `calendar_event_id` stored per task to link back to the Calendar event for updates and deletes.

## API Design

- `GET /tasks/for-sync` — artifact sync endpoint, not a general list
- `GET /tasks` — full list (admin/debug use)
- `POST /tasks/smart-create` — creates task, auto-detects reminder vs time_block
- `PATCH /tasks/:id` — update specific fields, whitelist-protected
- `POST /tasks/:id/complete` — mark done, record actual_minutes
- `POST /tasks/:id/archive` — soft delete
- No hard delete endpoint.

## Skills

### /create-task
- Ask for any missing fields conversationally (one at a time, not all at once).
- Required: title.
- Ask if missing: due date/time, estimated time, priority (default 3), recurring.
- Optional: description.
- Show confirmation summary before saving.
- On confirm: call `create_task` MCP → get taskId → call `gcal_create_event` → get calendar_event_id → call `patch_task` to link calendar_event_id back to DB.

### /sync-calendar
- Read `tasks-artifact` from AI-Productivity-Assistant Claude project. Create it if missing.
- Call `gcal_list_events` for window: -3 days to +7 days, timezone Australia/Melbourne.
- For each event: skip if no `[task]` block in description.
- Parse `[task]` block. Detect `[done]` prefix → set status done.
- Merge into artifact: Calendar wins on all fields.
- Preserve local-only tasks (no calendar_event_id, not in Calendar).
- Separate active tasks (`tasks[]`) from completed (`completed[]`).
- Write updated artifact back to Claude project.
- Report summary: synced, added, done, preserved.
